  "description": [
    {
      "value": "<p>A short hafted striker with a head of dense water ice cast around a bone core, used to sound bedding planes and to speak along them. The ice head is renewed constantly and this one was cast, recorded and frozen within the hour; what survives in the collection is the bone core, the haft, and a mould made at the time. The haft is polished to a deep shine at the grip and is not polished anywhere else, which is a good guide to how the tool is held. Sound tests on the reconstruction reproduce the recorded strikes to within a few per cent, which the acoustics group regards as settled and the tenders have never been asked about.</p>",
      "inLanguage": [{ "id": ["core.peerdb.org", "LANGUAGE", "en-GB"] }]
    }
